<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia's Jan 1-20 palm oil exports 302,702t - SGS.</title>
<headline>Malaysia's Jan 1-20 palm oil exports 302,702t - SGS.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo surveyor Societe Generale de Surveillance (SGS) Malaysia Sdn Bhd said it estimated Malaysia's palm oil exports for January 1-20 at 302,702 tonnes against 468,439 in December 1-20.</p>
<p>It said the exports comprised 60,894 tonnes of RBD palm oil, 122,966 tonnes of RBD palm olein and 44,589 tonnes of RBD palm stearin. The other products were 74,253 tonnes.</p>
<p>India, which was the main buyer during the period, taking 65,950 tonnes, Pakistan 25,072 tonnes, China 20,125 tonnes and Indonesia 17,660.</p>
<p>Countries in the European Union bought 73,995 tonnes. -- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230-8911)</p>
</text>
